    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "If we know the meaning of trigonometric function, then we could just recall that $\\sin A= \\tfrac{a}{c}$ where $a$ is the length of side opposite to angle $A$ and $c$ is the hypotenuse.  Looking at triangle $ABC$, $a = AB$ and $c = BC$, so $\\sin 90^\\circ = \\tfrac{16}{24} = \\tfrac{2}{3}$.",
