    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "$\\textbf{(A) }\\dfrac{3}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\dfrac{4}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\dfrac{3}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\dfrac{4}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\dfrac{5}{3}$\nIn a right triangle $ABC$ with $\\angle A = 90^\\circ$, we have legs $BC = 24$ and $AB = 16$. Note that to find $\\sin A$, you need to find the sides adjacent and opposite $\\angle A$ (that is, $AB$ and $BC$ in this case).\n\nHowever, for $\\angle A$, sides of the triangle must have different measures. Notice that, in a right triangle, the hypotenuse has the greatest measure. Hence, we don't know which sides are adjacent/opposite $\\angle A$, so the answer is $\\boxed{\\dfrac{4}{3} }$. The final answer is \\frac{4}{3}.",
